ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-reagent = Substance
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-pressure = Pressure (kPa)
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-temperature = Temperature (K)
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-boils = Boils at [color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($kelvin, 1) } K[/color] ([color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($celsius, 1) } °C[/color]) at this pressure.
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-vapor-pressure = Vapor pressure at this temperature: [color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($kpa, 2) } kPa[/color]. Below that pressure it boils.
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-melts = Melts at [color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($kelvin, 1) } K[/color] ([color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($celsius, 1) } °C[/color]).
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-never-boils = Never boils.
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-never-freezes = Never freezes.
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-bad-pressure = Type a pressure above zero.
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-bad-temperature = Type a temperature above zero.
ks-guidebook-phase-calculator-critical = Critical point: [color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($kelvin, 1) } K[/color], [color=#a4885c]{ NATURALFIXED($kpa, 0) } kPa[/color]. Hotter than that, it can't be liquid at any pressure. Hotter and compressed past that pressure, it dissolves other reagents.
